      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "$$\nC={1,2,…,100},\\,D={2n∣\\,n\\in Z}\n$$\n\nComplete the following reasoning about the sets $C$ and $D$ above:",
      "worked_solution": "The cardinalities of two sets cannot be equal if one set is finite and the other is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, notice that \n\n- $C$ is finite where $|C|=100,$  while\n\n- $D={…,-4,-2,0,2,4,…}$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, $|C|\\ne |D|.$",
